 r"I am writing to apply for the Associate Analyst role in Nectar360 Supplier Analytics. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. The role you describe, using SQL on large customer datasets to answer real business questions and then explaining the answer clearly to clients, is very close to the work I enjoy most.",

 r"What draws me to Nectar360 is the chance to see recommendations used in the real world. With more than 27 million Nectar members, the data can show how customers actually behave, and the supplier work means the insight goes straight to the people who decide on ranging, promotions and campaigns. I like taking a loosely framed question, working out what the stakeholder really needs to know, and turning it into an analysis they can act on.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I query large merchant and transaction tables in SQL and Python to find what is driving performance across the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. I present my findings to these teams directly, so I have learned to lead with the recommendation and keep the technical detail for anyone who wants it. When my supervisor asked me to set up a merchant campaign configuration by hand, I used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked with a pharmaceutical client and their clinical experts to agree what a good answer from their AI product looked like, built a 246-question benchmark the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and presented the results and recommendations to their team. At Ipsos Strategy3 I turned more than 80 interviews into quantitative customer insight and built forecasting models, then turned the results into dashboards and presentations for client stakeholders.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, comparing predictive models and estimating the effect of lifestyle changes with causal methods, which gave me a lot of practice with large datasets, careful statistics and checking results before reporting them. I would bring Nectar360 strong SQL and Python, sound statistics, experience with dashboards and client presentations, and real curiosity about customer behaviour. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am based in London.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I could contribute to the Nectar360 Supplier Analytics team.",
